# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js 16.1.6 project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 1.3.1
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with dependency resolutions

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `web/src/app/layout.tsx`**
- Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the `{children}` wrapped in `<Providers>`
- Placement ensures Speed Insights loads properly while maintaining existing app structure

## Implementation Details

This Next.js project uses:
- **Next.js Version**: 16.1.6 (App Router)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Router Type**: App Router

Since the project uses Next.js 16.1.6 with the App Router, I followed the recommended approach:
1. Used the `/next` import path for automatic routing detection
2. Added the component directly to the root layout
3. No additional configuration needed - the component will automatically track route changes

## Verification

✅ Package successfully installed
